00:25:00.000 --> 00:25:01.520
despite her unfortunate relations,

00:25:01.920 --> 00:25:03.760
and I should not be sorry to know her better.

00:25:04.000 --> 00:25:05.380
No, no, nor I.

00:25:05.760 --> 00:25:08.620
You see, Mr. Darcy, we are not afraid of you.

00:25:09.080 --> 00:25:10.080
I would not have you, sir.

00:25:14.910 --> 00:25:17.850
Ah, very true. Damn tedious waste of an evening.

00:25:19.900 --> 00:25:22.040
He's just what a young man ought to be, Lizzie.

00:25:23.160 --> 00:25:27.930
Sensible, lively, and I never saw such happy manners.

00:25:28.590 --> 00:25:29.970
Handsome, too, which a young man...

00:25:30.460 --> 00:25:34.520
And he seems to like you very much, which shows good judgment.

00:25:35.480 --> 00:25:38.100
No, I give you leave to like him. You've liked many a stupider person.

00:25:38.800 --> 00:25:39.600
Dear Lizzie.

00:25:41.180 --> 00:25:43.510
He and his choice of sisters and friends.

00:25:43.730 --> 00:25:45.370
Though the sisters, I suppose, he cannot help.

00:25:45.600 --> 00:25:46.380
Do you not like them?

00:25:46.540 --> 00:25:49.500
Not at all. Their manners are quite different from his.

00:25:49.990 --> 00:25:52.830
At first, perhaps. But after a while, I found them very pleasing.

00:25:53.580 --> 00:25:55.140
Miss Bingley is to keep house for her brother.

00:25:55.340 --> 00:25:57.320
And I'm sure they will be very charming neighbours.

00:25:57.750 --> 00:25:58.690
One of them, maybe.

00:26:00.250 --> 00:26:05.940
no lizzie i'm sure you're wrong and even mr darcy you know may improve on closer acquaintance

00:26:05.940 --> 00:26:10.180
do you mean he'll be in humor to give consequence to young ladies who are slighted by other men

00:26:10.770 --> 00:26:21.720
never she is tolerable i suppose not handsome enough to tempt me it was very wrong of him to

00:26:21.720 --> 00:26:25.680
speaks. Indeed it was. Little offence.

00:26:28.310 --> 00:26:28.930
Well it is calm.

00:26:41.970 --> 00:26:47.300
I hope this will be the first of many occasions when Lucas Lodge will be graced with your

00:26:47.300 --> 00:26:54.100
presence. Here you see we're all easy with no awkwardness or ceremony. Quite. Oh yes,

00:26:54.320 --> 00:26:59.620
my dear. Five thousand a year. Don't they look well, dear?

00:27:00.440 --> 00:27:03.120
Just agreeable, young man.

00:27:05.210 --> 00:27:07.210
Now, children, I want to introduce you to you.

00:27:07.840 --> 00:27:11.260
Sir, this is Captain Hartford.

00:27:14.700 --> 00:27:17.940
And he would dance every dance with Jane.

00:27:18.220 --> 00:27:19.240
Nothing else would do.

00:27:19.500 --> 00:27:22.640
And are you pleased with Hartfordshire, Colonel Forster?

00:27:22.780 --> 00:27:23.880
Very much so, Lady Lucas.

00:27:24.160 --> 00:27:25.500
And ever more so than this evening.

00:27:25.880 --> 00:27:29.200
The regiment of infantry doesn't find a ready welcome everywhere, I fear.

00:27:29.320 --> 00:27:29.980
I think you're...

00:27:30.030 --> 00:27:31.910
officers will be very well pleased with

00:27:31.910 --> 00:27:32.250
merits.

00:27:35.870 --> 00:27:37.850
Denny and Sarteson seem well pleased

00:27:37.850 --> 00:27:38.310
already.

00:27:39.510 --> 00:27:41.650
No doubt you attend assemblies at

00:27:41.650 --> 00:27:43.170
St. James's Court, Miss Bingley.

00:27:43.450 --> 00:27:45.800
We go but rarely, sir. Indeed,

00:27:45.820 --> 00:27:48.440
I am surprised. I should be

00:27:48.440 --> 00:27:50.280
happy to introduce you there, you know,

00:27:50.300 --> 00:27:51.880
at any time when I'm in town.

00:27:53.300 --> 00:27:54.560
You're too kind, sir.

00:27:57.760 --> 00:27:59.970
Well, well, good.

00:28:00.250 --> 00:28:09.620
good insufferable conceit to imagine that we'd need his assistance in society

00:28:10.320 --> 00:28:15.920
i am sure he is a very good sort of man caroline and i am sure he kept a very good sort of shop

00:28:15.920 --> 00:28:17.920
before his elevation to the knighthood

00:28:22.090 --> 00:28:24.600
he must be suffering

00:28:44.360 --> 00:28:48.160
Are you a Meryton to subdue the discontented populace, sir,

00:28:48.300 --> 00:28:50.340
or do you defend Hertfordshire against the French?

00:28:50.720 --> 00:28:51.880
Neither ma'am, I trust.

00:28:52.460 --> 00:28:54.220
We hope to winter very peacefully at Meryton.

00:28:54.440 --> 00:28:56.240
My soldiers are in great need of training,

00:28:56.540 --> 00:28:59.160
and my officers in ever great need of society.

00:29:00.960 --> 00:29:03.120
Then as soon as you are settled, I hope you will give a ball.

00:29:03.640 --> 00:29:05.140
Oh, yes, my dear, do.

00:29:05.460 --> 00:29:07.180
You think a ball would be well received?

00:29:07.400 --> 00:29:09.400
A ball? Who's giving a ball?

00:29:09.500 --> 00:29:11.460
I long for a ball, and so does Denny.

00:29:11.500 --> 00:29:12.920
I'm Sanderson, don't you, Sanderson?

00:29:13.040 --> 00:29:16.360
I do indeed, most passionately.

00:29:16.700 --> 00:29:18.980
Ah, little Sanderson, I knew you would.

00:29:19.080 --> 00:29:20.460
Make him give a ball, Mrs. Foster.

00:29:20.720 --> 00:29:21.940
We'll dance with all the officers.

00:29:22.360 --> 00:29:25.340
But if Mary would only play something, we could dance with them now.

00:29:26.070 --> 00:29:28.590
Mary! Mary, let's have no more of that dull stuff.

00:29:28.690 --> 00:29:29.970
Play something jolly. We want to...

00:29:30.440 --> 00:29:32.160
But there are still two movements.

00:29:32.730 --> 00:29:34.740
Mama, tell them it isn't fair.

00:29:35.600 --> 00:29:39.170
Oh, play a jig, Mary. No one wants your concertos here.

00:29:42.300 --> 00:29:45.640
I fear their taste is not as fine as yours and mine, Mary,

00:29:45.780 --> 00:29:47.560
but let us oblige them this once, eh?

00:29:47.840 --> 00:29:50.600
For there is no one here who plays as well as you.

00:29:51.680 --> 00:29:55.050
Very well. Though you know it gives me little pleasure.

00:29:56.440 --> 00:29:58.600
Jane, Mr Bingley, come and dance with us.

00:29:58.620 --> 00:29:59.120
Not now, Lydia.

00:30:01.050 --> 00:30:16.800
I see that Mr. Bingley continues his attentions to Jane, Lizzie.

00:30:20.490 --> 00:30:22.150
I'm very happy for her, Charlotte.

00:30:22.840 --> 00:30:24.660
She does seem very well pleased with him.

00:30:25.420 --> 00:30:28.480
I think if he continues so, she's in a fair way to be very much in love with him.

00:30:29.430 --> 00:30:29.970
And Mr. Bingley...

00:30:30.000 --> 00:30:31.660
Mr. Bingley, do you think he is in love?

00:30:33.660 --> 00:30:35.720
It's clear that he likes her very much.

00:30:36.160 --> 00:30:38.440
Then she should leave him in no doubt of her heart.

00:30:38.860 --> 00:30:41.680
She should show more affection even than she feels,

00:30:41.720 --> 00:30:43.560
not less if she is to secure him.

00:30:43.860 --> 00:30:45.330
To cure him?

00:30:45.920 --> 00:30:49.180
Oh, yes. She should secure him as soon as may be.

00:30:50.930 --> 00:30:52.970
Before she is short of his character,

00:30:53.130 --> 00:30:55.110
before she's even certain of her own regard for him.

00:30:55.230 --> 00:30:55.890
But of course.

00:30:57.060 --> 00:30:59.860
Happiness in marriage is entirely a matter of chance, you know.

00:31:00.030 --> 00:31:08.420
There will always be vexation and grief and it is better to know in advance as little as possible of the defects of your marriage partner

00:31:08.420 --> 00:31:09.550
She did not know

00:31:10.050 --> 00:31:13.490
You know it is not sound you would never act like that yourself

00:31:13.490 --> 00:31:17.620
Well, it seems that Jane will not so we must hope that mr. Bingley will

00:31:17.620 --> 00:31:29.980
I think he gets little encouragement from his sisters or his friend mr. Darcy

00:31:30.000 --> 00:31:31.380
he looks at you a great deal, is he?

00:31:31.400 --> 00:31:32.600
I cannot think why.

00:31:33.080 --> 00:31:34.900
Unless he means to frighten me with his contempt.

00:31:35.980 --> 00:31:37.660
I wish he would not come into society.

00:31:37.920 --> 00:31:38.980
He only makes people uneasy.

00:31:40.280 --> 00:31:43.280
What a charming amusement

00:31:43.280 --> 00:31:45.400
for young people this is, Mr. Darcy.

00:31:45.900 --> 00:31:47.320
Nothing like dancing,

00:31:47.580 --> 00:31:49.440
you know. One of the refinements

00:31:49.440 --> 00:31:50.900
in every polished society.

00:31:51.140 --> 00:31:52.860
And every unpolished society.

00:31:53.550 --> 00:31:56.020
So? Every savage can dance.

00:31:57.150 --> 00:31:58.060
Oh, yeah.

00:31:59.080 --> 00:31:59.740
It's quite...

00:32:01.670 --> 00:32:06.530
I think I should speak to my sister before she exposes us all to ridicule.

00:32:12.350 --> 00:32:15.840
Miss Eliza, why are you not dancing?

00:32:16.460 --> 00:32:21.440
Mr. Darcy, allow me to present this young lady to you as a very desirable partner.

00:32:22.220 --> 00:32:26.320
You cannot refuse to dance, I'm sure, when so much beauty is before you.

00:32:26.740 --> 00:32:29.080
Indeed, sir, I've not the least intention of dancing.

00:32:30.000 --> 00:32:33.460
Please don't suppose that I move this way in order to beg for a partner.

00:32:33.900 --> 00:32:37.740
I would be very happy if you would do me the honor of dancing with me, Miss Bennett.

00:32:38.460 --> 00:32:43.510
Thank you, but excuse me, I am not inclined to dance.

00:32:43.850 --> 00:32:45.030
Come, come, why not?

00:32:45.360 --> 00:32:50.700
When you see Mr. Darcy has no objection, although he dislikes the amusement so much in general.

00:32:51.100 --> 00:32:52.860
Mr. Darcy is all politeness.

00:32:52.900 --> 00:32:54.060
He is, he is.

00:32:54.280 --> 00:32:57.120
And why should he not be considering the inducement?

00:32:57.700 --> 00:32:59.780
For who could object to such a partner?

00:33:00.000 --> 00:33:00.560
Hey, Darcy.

00:33:00.980 --> 00:33:02.240
Beg you would excuse me.

00:33:03.720 --> 00:33:04.750
Well, well.

00:33:05.310 --> 00:33:07.370
Oh, capital, Lydia, capital.

00:33:12.840 --> 00:33:16.840
I believe I can guess your thoughts at this moment.

00:33:18.570 --> 00:33:19.670
I should imagine not.

00:33:21.940 --> 00:33:24.700
You are thinking how insupportable it would be

00:33:24.700 --> 00:33:27.750
to spend many evenings in such tea as company.

00:33:28.720 --> 00:33:29.960
No, indeed, my mind was.

00:33:30.380 --> 00:33:35.170
agreeably engaged. I've been meditating on the very great pleasure which a pair of fine

00:33:35.170 --> 00:33:42.300
eyes in the face of a pretty woman can bestow. May one dare ask

00:33:42.300 --> 00:33:45.730
whose are the eyes that inspired these reflections?

00:33:46.520 --> 00:33:58.410
Miss Elizabeth Bennet's. Bennet? Well, astonishment.

00:34:00.160 --> 00:34:09.570
What does it say?

00:34:10.220 --> 00:34:11.240
It is from Miss Bingley.

00:34:11.660 --> 00:34:15.090
Oh, well, that is a good sign, too.

00:34:16.370 --> 00:34:20.710
Give it to me, my dear friend.

00:34:21.830 --> 00:34:25.740
There, now, with Louisa and me today.

00:34:26.640 --> 00:34:29.750
La-dee-da, la-dee-da, la-dee-da, la-dee-da.

00:34:30.190 --> 00:34:32.530
as the gentlemen are to dine with the officers.

00:34:32.750 --> 00:34:33.470
Oh, that's unlucky.

00:34:34.240 --> 00:34:36.340
Still, you must go and make what you can of it.

00:34:37.020 --> 00:34:39.590
Yours ever, Caroline Bingley.

00:34:39.830 --> 00:34:41.390
Very elegant hand.

00:34:41.710 --> 00:34:43.010
May I have a carriage, Father?

00:34:44.270 --> 00:34:47.550
Carriage? You must go on horseback,

00:34:48.060 --> 00:34:49.120
for it looks like rain.

00:34:49.380 --> 00:34:50.600
Then you will have to stay the night.

00:34:51.660 --> 00:34:52.060
Mother!

00:34:52.380 --> 00:34:55.140
Why do you look at me like that?

00:34:55.240 --> 00:34:56.880
Would you go all the way to Netherfield and back

00:34:56.880 --> 00:34:58.100
without seeing Mr Bingley?

00:34:58.570 --> 00:34:59.070
No, indeed.

00:35:00.250 --> 00:35:02.430
You will go on, Nellie. That will do very well indeed.

00:35:20.000 --> 00:35:25.440
Lizzie, you see? It is all exactly as I planned.

00:35:42.250 --> 00:35:45.850
Now, let me see if I've got this right, Jane.

00:35:46.920 --> 00:35:50.470
Your mother's sister is named Mrs. Phillips.

00:35:52.620 --> 00:35:55.660
And Mr. Phillips' estate is, um...

00:35:56.610 --> 00:35:57.830
He lives in Meryton.

00:35:59.390 --> 00:35:59.970
He's an attorney.

00:36:00.000 --> 00:36:07.800
And your mother's brother lives in London?

00:36:09.630 --> 00:36:12.480
Yeah, in Grace Church Street.

00:36:14.040 --> 00:36:17.560
In which part of London is Grace Church Street, Jane?

00:36:18.630 --> 00:36:18.950
I...

00:36:27.200 --> 00:36:29.120
Fawcett, get help. Miss Bennet is unwell.

00:36:33.550 --> 00:36:37.470
Well, my dear, if Jane should die of this fever,

00:36:38.200 --> 00:36:41.240
it would be comfort to know that it was all in pursuit of Mr Bingley

00:36:41.240 --> 00:36:42.980
and under your orders.

00:36:43.920 --> 00:36:48.030
Nonsense. People do not die of little trifling colds.

00:36:49.070 --> 00:36:50.750
She will be very well taken care of.

00:36:50.770 --> 00:36:52.510
Mama, I think I must go to Netherfield.

00:36:55.380 --> 00:36:58.140
Call for that. Jane is very well where she is.

00:36:58.260 --> 00:36:59.970
There is nothing for you.

00:37:00.000 --> 00:37:02.770
you at Netherfield. You had much better

00:37:02.770 --> 00:37:04.790
go to Meryton with your sisters and meet the officers.

00:37:05.460 --> 00:37:06.900
Aye, Lizzie, for there are more than enough

00:37:06.900 --> 00:37:10.120
to go round. I know that Jane

00:37:10.120 --> 00:37:12.920
would wish me to be with her. I suppose

00:37:12.920 --> 00:37:15.120
that is a hint for me to send for the carriage.

00:37:16.270 --> 00:37:17.850
Oh, no, indeed, Father, for I had

00:37:17.850 --> 00:37:20.010
much rather walk. It is

00:37:20.010 --> 00:37:22.050
barely three miles to Netherfield, and

00:37:22.050 --> 00:37:23.570
I'll be back for dinner.

00:37:25.020 --> 00:37:28.100
Three miles in all that? You'll not be fit

00:37:28.100 --> 00:37:29.930
to be seen. I shall be

00:37:30.000 --> 00:37:34.680
I'm not fit to see Jane, which is all I want. I'm quite determined, Mother.

00:37:35.780 --> 00:37:38.290
I know, Lizzie. Lydia and I will set you as far as Meryton.

00:37:38.770 --> 00:37:43.030
Aye, let's call on Denny early before he is dressed. What shock he will get.

00:37:45.190 --> 00:37:47.850
Our life holds few distinctions, Mrs. Bennet,

00:37:47.990 --> 00:37:52.470
but I think we may safely boast that here sit two of the silliest girls in the country.

00:38:48.630 --> 00:38:54.150
I am come to inquire after my sister.

00:38:56.260 --> 00:38:56.760
On foot.

00:38:58.060 --> 00:38:58.540
As you see.

00:39:03.390 --> 00:39:05.450
Would you be so kind as to take me to her?

00:39:33.200 --> 00:39:37.530
Well, we must allow her to be an excellent walker, I suppose.

00:39:39.140 --> 00:39:42.440
Appearance this morning. She really looked almost wild.

00:39:43.450 --> 00:39:44.950
Hardly keep my countenance.

00:39:45.070 --> 00:39:49.300
What does she mean by scampering about the country because her sister has a cold?

00:39:50.080 --> 00:39:51.440
Her hair, Louisa.

00:39:51.750 --> 00:39:55.260
Her petticoat. I hope you saw her petticoat, brother.

00:39:55.720 --> 00:39:58.180
Six inches deep in mud, I'm absolutely certain.

00:39:58.380 --> 00:39:59.980
I must confess it quite escaped my notice.

00:40:00.000 --> 00:40:01.620
I thought she looked remarkably well.

00:40:02.470 --> 00:40:05.070
You observed it, I'm sure, Mr. Darcy.

00:40:05.700 --> 00:40:06.100
I did.

00:40:07.240 --> 00:40:10.860
I'm inclined to think you wouldn't wish your sister to make such an exhibition.

00:40:11.590 --> 00:40:12.190
Certainly not.

00:40:14.380 --> 00:40:19.360
Seems to me to show an abominable sort of conceited independence.

00:40:20.130 --> 00:40:22.790
Shows an affection for her sister that is very pleasing.

00:40:23.370 --> 00:40:29.750
I'm afraid, Mr. Darcy, that this escapade may have affected your admiration for her fine eyes.

00:40:30.670 --> 00:40:32.850
Not at all. They were brightened by the exercise.

00:40:38.150 --> 00:40:40.250
Jane Bennett is a sweet girl.

00:40:41.270 --> 00:40:43.770
It's very sad she should have such an unfortunate family.

00:40:44.010 --> 00:40:45.050
Such low connections.

00:40:45.600 --> 00:40:49.980
Their uncle, she told us, is in trade and lives in Cheapside.

00:40:50.810 --> 00:40:53.170
Well, perhaps we should call when we are next in town.

00:40:55.590 --> 00:40:59.980
They would be just as agreeable to me had they uncles enough to fill all...

00:41:00.000 --> 00:41:04.240
With such connections, they can have very little chance of marrying well, Bingley.

00:41:05.090 --> 00:41:06.610
That is the material point.

00:41:11.960 --> 00:41:15.400
Miss Barrett, how does your sister do? Is she any better?

00:41:15.900 --> 00:41:18.100
I'm afraid that she's quite unwell, Mr Bingley.

00:41:19.030 --> 00:41:22.090
Let me send for Mr Jones, and you must stay until your sister is recovered.

00:41:22.570 --> 00:41:24.410
I would not wish to inconvenience you.

00:41:24.820 --> 00:41:28.280
I wouldn't care of anything else. I'll send to Longbourn for your clothes directly.

00:41:29.340 --> 00:41:29.860
Very kind.

00:41:30.700 --> 00:41:32.340
It's been a very sport today or not.

00:42:16.670 --> 00:42:17.850
I disgrace you, do you think?

00:42:19.590 --> 00:42:22.840
You look very pretty, Lizzie, as you are well aware.

00:42:24.340 --> 00:42:29.960
Oh, Jane, I'd much rather stay here with you, the superior...

00:42:30.060 --> 00:42:31.820
sisters wish me miles

00:42:31.820 --> 00:42:34.140
away. Only your Mr. Bingley

00:42:34.140 --> 00:42:35.780
is civil and attentive.

00:42:37.080 --> 00:42:38.800
He is not my Mr. Bingley,

00:42:38.920 --> 00:42:40.920
Lizzie. Oh, I think he is.

00:42:41.120 --> 00:42:44.610
Or he very soon will be.

00:42:45.500 --> 00:42:59.560
I believe you will find Mr. Bingley

00:42:59.560 --> 00:42:59.980
isn't the...

00:43:00.030 --> 00:43:02.090
drawing. Thank you.

00:43:37.610 --> 00:43:41.450
Mr. Darcy, come and advise me. For Mr. Hurst, Carrie's all before him.

00:43:43.030 --> 00:43:51.920
I inquire after your sister, Miss Bennet.

00:43:53.340 --> 00:43:55.340
Aye, thank you. I believe she's a little better.

00:43:56.440 --> 00:43:57.320
I'm very glad to hear it.

00:43:58.330 --> 00:43:59.890
No, Miss, I'm quite undone.

00:44:00.508 --> 00:44:01.688
Should have played with a deuce.

00:44:01.988 --> 00:44:03.828
He's undone as always, Mr. Darcy.

00:44:06.556 --> 00:44:08.556
Will you join us, Ms. Bennet?

00:44:09.180 --> 00:44:10.180
Thank you, no.

00:44:10.716 --> 00:44:12.456
You prefer reading to cards, do?

00:44:13.180 --> 00:44:19.180
singular miss bennett despises card she's a great reader and has no pleasure in anything else

00:44:21.148 --> 00:44:24.288
I deserve neither such praise nor such censure.

00:44:24.488 --> 00:44:27.608
I am not a great reader and take pleasure in many things.

00:44:30.320 --> 00:44:32.480
And what do you do so secretly, sir?

00:44:32.780 --> 00:44:40.200
It is no secret. I'm writing to my sister.

00:44:40.740 --> 00:44:46.370
Oh, do you see her? Is she much grown since the spring?

00:44:46.830 --> 00:44:47.910
Is she as tall as me?

00:44:49.110 --> 00:44:52.910
It's now about Miss Elizabeth Bennet's height.

00:44:53.910 --> 00:44:54.650
We're a little taller.

00:44:55.430 --> 00:44:59.630
And so accomplished. Her performance at the Piano Forti is exquisite.

00:45:00.670 --> 00:45:01.890
Do you play, Miss Bennet?

00:45:02.230 --> 00:45:03.590
I am a very ill indeed.

00:45:03.930 --> 00:45:05.700
But all young ladies are accomplished.

00:45:06.020 --> 00:45:08.270
They sing, they draw, they dance,

00:45:08.430 --> 00:45:10.280
speak French and German,

00:45:10.420 --> 00:45:12.640
cover screens, and I know not what.

00:45:12.900 --> 00:45:14.980
There are not half a dozen who would sing.

00:45:15.000 --> 00:45:20.160
satisfy my notion of an accomplished woman? Oh, certainly. No woman can be really esteemed

00:45:20.160 --> 00:45:25.830
accomplished who does not also possess a certain something in her air, in the manner of walking,

00:45:26.090 --> 00:45:29.150
in the tone of her voice, her address and expressions.

00:45:30.764 --> 00:45:33.104
And to all this, she must yet add something more substantial.

00:45:34.540 --> 00:45:37.160
and the improvement of her mind by extensive reading.

00:45:39.276 --> 00:45:41.816
I'm no longer surprised at you knowing only...

00:45:42.284 --> 00:45:44.184
Six accomplished women, Mr. Darcy.

00:45:44.304 --> 00:45:44.564
Aye.

00:45:44.748 --> 00:45:46.188
rather wonder you're knowing any.

00:45:46.892 --> 00:45:49.892
You are very severe upon your sex, Miss Bennet.

00:45:50.796 --> 00:45:51.756
You must speak as I find.

00:45:52.204 --> 00:45:57.104
Perhaps you have not had the advantage, Miss Bennet, of moving in society enough.

00:45:57.344 --> 00:45:59.924
There are many very accomplished young ladies.

00:46:00.000 --> 00:46:01.540
amongst our acquaintance.

00:46:01.884 --> 00:46:04.724
Come, come, this is a fine way to play a cardinal or light.

00:46:05.340 --> 00:46:05.840
Thank you.

00:46:14.428 --> 00:46:14.928
Don't go!

00:46:15.388 --> 00:46:16.908
Is it not a fair prospect?

00:46:29.500 --> 00:46:30.000
Another month.

00:46:31.116 --> 00:46:34.116
Are we to be invaded by every Bennet in the country?

00:46:34.316 --> 00:46:36.316
It's too much to be born.

00:46:42.732 --> 00:46:44.732
Mrs. Bennet, you are very welcome.

00:46:44.908 --> 00:46:47.368
I hope you do not find Miss Bennet worse than you expected.

00:46:47.568 --> 00:46:48.648
Indeed I do, sir.

00:46:48.828 --> 00:46:51.948
She is very ill indeed and suffers a vast deal.

00:46:52.300 --> 00:46:54.320
Though with the greatest patience in the world.

00:46:54.600 --> 00:46:56.940
For she has the sweetest temper, Mr Bingley.

00:46:57.280 --> 00:46:59.800
But she is a great deal too ill to be moved.

00:47:00.540 --> 00:47:03.400
We must trespass a little longer on your kindness.

00:47:04.604 --> 00:47:05.304
But of course.

00:47:06.332 --> 00:47:09.512
Miss Bennet will receive every possible attention, ma'am.

00:47:09.660 --> 00:47:10.440
I assure you.

00:47:10.620 --> 00:47:11.900
You are very good.

00:47:13.596 --> 00:47:16.816
Well, you have a sweet room here.

00:47:17.296 --> 00:47:20.536
I think you will never want to leave Netherfield now you are come here.

00:47:21.148 --> 00:47:23.408
I believe I should be happy to live in the country forever.

00:47:23.868 --> 00:47:24.628
Wouldn't you, Darcy?

00:47:25.756 --> 00:47:26.156
You would.

00:47:27.036 --> 00:47:29.776
You don't find the society somewhat confined and unvarying.

00:47:30.000 --> 00:47:38.720
taste. Indeed it is not, sir. The country is a vast deal pleasanter than town, whatever you may say about it.

00:47:41.790 --> 00:47:44.150
Mama, you've misstaked Mr. Darcy's meaning.

00:47:45.890 --> 00:47:50.710
He seems to think the country not all can find unvarying.

00:47:50.710 --> 00:47:54.230
I would have him know we dine with four and twenty families.

00:48:02.590 --> 00:48:06.170
Mama, have you seen Charlotte Lucas since I came away?

00:48:07.000 --> 00:48:08.900
Yes, she called yesterday with Sir William.

00:48:09.790 --> 00:48:11.730
What an agreeable man he is.

00:48:12.010 --> 00:48:14.090
That is my idea of good breeding.

00:48:14.640 --> 00:48:18.040
And those persons who fancy themselves very important

00:48:18.040 --> 00:48:21.160
and never open their mouths quite mistake the matter.

00:48:24.140 --> 00:48:26.160
Did you not promise to give a ball at Netherfield

00:48:26.160 --> 00:48:27.320
as soon as you were settled here?

00:48:27.460 --> 00:48:29.960
It will be a great scandal if you don't keep your word.

00:48:30.640 --> 00:48:32.420
I'm perfectly ready to keep my engagement.

00:48:32.880 --> 00:48:34.140
And when your sister has recovered,

00:48:34.860 --> 00:48:36.640
you shall name the day of the ball, if you please.

00:48:37.460 --> 00:48:42.120
How is this a fair promise for you?

00:48:42.400 --> 00:48:44.420
That's generosity for you.

00:48:47.580 --> 00:48:50.410
What I call gentlemanly behavior.

00:50:00.350 --> 00:50:00.610
Oh

00:50:44.080 --> 00:50:47.770
I persuade you to follow my example

00:50:47.770 --> 00:50:49.310
and take a turn about the room.

00:50:49.430 --> 00:50:50.290
It's so refreshing.

00:51:03.480 --> 00:51:11.590
not join us, Mr. Darcy? That would defeat the object. What do you mean, sir? What on earth can

00:51:11.590 --> 00:51:19.450
he mean? I think we would do better not to inquire. May we insist on knowing your meaning, sir? Why,

00:51:19.510 --> 00:51:23.330
that your figures appear to best advantage when walking, and that I might best admire them from

00:51:23.330 --> 00:51:29.970
my present position. Shall we punish him, Miss Eliza?

00:51:30.320 --> 00:51:32.380
nothing so easy

00:51:32.380 --> 00:51:33.910
tease him

00:51:34.990 --> 00:51:35.890
laugh at him

00:51:36.840 --> 00:51:38.000
laugh at Mr. Darcy

00:51:39.530 --> 00:51:39.890
impossible

00:51:39.890 --> 00:51:43.250
he is a man without fault

00:51:44.010 --> 00:51:45.070
is he indeed

00:51:45.070 --> 00:51:48.100
a man without fault

00:51:48.100 --> 00:51:51.000
that is not possible for anyone

00:51:51.000 --> 00:51:54.990
but it has been my study to avoid those weaknesses

00:51:54.990 --> 00:51:57.130
which expose a strong understanding to ridicule

00:51:58.790 --> 00:51:59.890
such as a

00:52:00.000 --> 00:52:02.160
Vanity, perhaps, and pride.

00:52:05.840 --> 00:52:07.240
Yes, vanity is a weakness indeed.

00:52:09.430 --> 00:52:14.050
But pride, where there is a real superiority of mine,

00:52:14.230 --> 00:52:15.610
pride will always be under good regulation.

00:52:15.790 --> 00:52:20.610
I have faults enough, Miss Bennet,

00:52:20.670 --> 00:52:21.950
but I hope they are not of understanding.

00:52:23.940 --> 00:52:25.180
A temper I cannot vouch for.

00:52:30.090 --> 00:52:36.780
be called resentful my good opinion once lost is lost forever that is a failing

00:52:36.780 --> 00:52:44.360
indeed but I cannot laugh at it I believe every disposition has a

00:52:44.360 --> 00:52:49.160
tendency to some particular evil your defect is a propensity to hate everyone

00:52:49.160 --> 00:52:52.880
while yours is willfully to misunderstand them shall we have some

00:52:52.880 --> 00:52:53.140
music

00:53:13.240 --> 00:53:15.080
Give your parents my warmest salutations

00:53:15.520 --> 00:53:18.360
and tell your father he's most welcome to come and shoot with us

00:53:18.360 --> 00:53:19.340
at any time convenient.

00:53:20.300 --> 00:53:21.740
Thank you, sir. You're very kind.

00:53:22.390 --> 00:53:22.790
Goodbye.

00:53:32.240 --> 00:53:33.000
Drive on, Roster.

00:53:34.310 --> 00:53:47.840
Listen, it is, to have one's has to oneself again.

00:53:51.560 --> 00:53:58.180
But I fear Mr. Darcy is mourning the loss of Miss Eliza Bennett's pert opinions and fine eyes.

00:54:00.570 --> 00:54:02.070
Quite the contrary, I'll show you.

00:54:11.120 --> 00:54:17.760
Jane, sorry to say it, but notwithstanding, you're excellent, Mr. Bingley.

00:54:18.020 --> 00:54:20.940
I've never been so happy to leave a place in my life.
